.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_POST_EVENT 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_post_event ,
.Nm ndi_busop_add_eventcall ,
.Nm ndi_busop_remove_eventcall ,
.Nm ndi_busop_get_eventcookie
.Nd dispatch event operations to a nexus driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_post_event
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "dev_info_t *rdip"
.Fa "ddi_eventcookie_t eventhdl"
.Fa "void *impl_data"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_busop_add_eventcall
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "dev_info_t *rdip"
.Fa "ddi_eventcookie_t eventhdl"
.Fa "void (*callback)()"
.Fa "void *arg"
.Fa "ddi_callback_id_t *cb_id"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_busop_remove_eventcall
.Fa "dev_info_t *ddip"
.Fa "ddi_callback_id_t id"
.Fc
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_busop_get_eventcookie
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "dev_info_t *rdip"
.Fa "char *name"
.Fa "ddi_eventcookie_t *event_cookiep"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va dip
Starting node for ancestor cookie lookup; ignored for posting and
callback registration.
.It Va rdip
Device requesting or receiving the event.
.It Va eventhdl
Valid event cookie identifying the responsible nexus.
.It Va impl_data
Event-specific data passed to the post operation.
.It Va callback
Event handler with the \fBddi_event_cb_f\fP calling convention.
.It Va arg
Opaque callback argument.
.It Va cb_id
Output for the registered callback identifier.
.It Va ddip
Nexus responsible for the callback being removed.
.It Va id
Live callback identifier.
.It Va name
Null-terminated event name.
.It Va event_cookiep
Output for the requested cookie.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions dispatch event operations through nexus bus operations.
The responsible nexus must provide the relevant event entry points with
\fBbusops_rev\fP at least \fBBUSO_REV_6\fP.
.Pp
\fBndi_post_event()\fP calls \fBbus_post_event\fP on the nexus identified by the
event cookie, passing the requesting node and implementation data.
\fBndi_busop_add_eventcall()\fP likewise calls that nexus's
\fBbus_add_eventcall\fP entry point and returns a callback identifier.
For these two functions, \fBdip\fP is retained for compatibility and is ignored;
the cookie selects the destination directly.
.Pp
\fBndi_busop_remove_eventcall()\fP calls \fBbus_remove_eventcall\fP on \fBddip\fP.
The caller must supply the nexus responsible for the live callback identifier.
.Pp
\fBndi_busop_get_eventcookie()\fP starts at the parent of \fBdip\fP and skips
ancestors that lack the required event-cookie operation or bus-operations
revision.
It calls the first suitable \fBbus_get_eventcookie\fP entry point, which may
itself forward a request it does not recognize.
It must not be called with the root as \fBdip\fP.
.Pp
Consumers normally use \fBddi_get_eventcookie()\fP, \fBddi_add_event_handler()\fP,
and \fBddi_remove_event_handler()\fP.
These NDI helpers support nexus implementations and framework dispatch.
Keep the participating nodes, driver operations, cookies, callback argument,
and implementation data valid for the operation and any registered callbacks.
.Sh CONTEXT
Cookie lookup and registration operations may be called from user or
kernel context.
Event posting must obey the context and priority contract of the event and
its nexus implementation.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The functions return the status of the invoked bus operation.
Registration or removal returns \fBDDI_FAILURE\fP when its required callback
operation is missing.
A valid cookie and a supported post operation are prerequisites for posting;
these are not arbitrary-handle validation interfaces.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ddi_add_event_handler 9F ,
.Xr ddi_get_eventcookie 9F ,
.Xr ddi_remove_event_handler 9F ,
.Xr ndi_event_add_callback 9F ,
.Xr ndi_event_retrieve_cookie 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F
